patch.description:
Partially updates an existing structure by modifying one or more of its properties.

As intended by the standard PATCH operation: there is no need to specify the complete set of data. Give only the data to change in the targeted ressource.

```json
{
    "label": "Research",
    "enabled": false
}
```

Beware of the following business rules, enforced on the whole subtree:
- disabling a structure also disables all its children;
- a structure holding active users cannot be disabled (**422**);
- a structure cannot be enabled while its parent is disabled: `enabled` is then forced to **false**;
- a department can be moved within its own company only, not to another one (**422**).

Patch action cannot be used to create a new structure. To create a structure, use the POST method instead.
